--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. THE CONTENT AND DATA  (source/, data/, and everything derived from them)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

NOT open. All rights reserved by their respective owners.

  * The ONFF reference boundaries originate from Belgian Flora & Fauna
    (ONFF), part of Belgium Outdoor Shack, and are distributed by them
    through their own channel. Diana renders them; Diana does not own them.
  * The underlying protected-area geometry derives from the World Database
    on Protected Areas (WDPA) and from Flemish and Walloon government
    sources, each with their own terms.
  * Activation figures come from the ONFF status sheet, maintained by the
    ONFF coordinator.
  * Live spots come from WWFF Spotline.

You may view this data through Diana. You may not redistribute it, republish
it, bulk-download it into another product, or reuse it in any other service,
without written permission from the ONFF coordinator.

A plain word about what that means in practice: the app has to send the zone
boundaries to every visitor's browser, because that is how a map works. This
notice does not change that, and it cannot technically prevent anyone from
saving the file. What it does is state the terms plainly, so that reuse is a
deliberate choice rather than an assumption. If you want this data for
another project, ask ONFF — they are approachable, and it is their work.

